        </thead>

        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry><guilabel>FeasibilityTolerance</guilabel></entry>

            <entry><para>Tolerance on the maximum violation of the supplied nonlinear constraints and bounds, used to determine feasibility. Choose constraint expressions with consistent numerical scaling; the optimizer does not automatically convert unlike physical units.</para> <variablelist>
                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Data Type</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Real</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Allowed Values</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Real &gt; 0</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Access</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>set</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Default Value</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>1e-4</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Units</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Constraint-residual numerical units; dimensionless only when the supplied constraints are nondimensional</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Interfaces</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>GUI, script</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>
              </variablelist></entry>
          </row>

          <row>
            <entry><guilabel>FunctionTolerance</guilabel></entry>

            <entry><para>Tolerance on the objective-change convergence metric. When the absolute previous cost exceeds 1e-7, the metric is the absolute relative change; otherwise it is the absolute change in objective value. This criterion also requires the feasibility check to pass.</para> <variablelist>
                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Data Type</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Real</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Allowed Values</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Real &gt; 0</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Access</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>set</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Default Value</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>1e-4</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Units</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Dimensionless relative objective change when abs(previous cost) exceeds 1e-7; objective-value units otherwise</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Interfaces</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>GUI, script</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>
              </variablelist></entry>
          </row>

          <row>
            <entry><guilabel>HessianUpdateMethod</guilabel></entry>

            <entry><para>The method used to approximate the Hessian of the
            Lagrangian. These methods are based on the BFGS but are more
            robust to possible numerical issues that can occur using BFGS
            updates with finite precision arithmetic. </para> <variablelist>
                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Data Type</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>String</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Allowed Values</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para><guilabel>DampedBFGS</guilabel>,
                    <guilabel>SelfScaledBFGS</guilabel></para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Access</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>set</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Default Value</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>
                      <guilabel>SelfScaledBFGS</guilabel>
                    </para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Units</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>None</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Interfaces</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>GUI, script</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>
              </variablelist></entry>
          </row>

          <row>
            <entry><guilabel>MaximumElasticWeight</guilabel></entry>

            <entry><para>Maximum penalty weight used when attempting to minimize infeasibility. Elastic mode adds the weighted sum of its elastic residual variables to the objective. The weight can grow by a factor of ten on unsuccessful iterations until the configured maximum is reached; it is a penalty limit, not an iteration count.</para> <variablelist>
                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Data Type</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Integer</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Allowed Values</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Integer &gt; 0</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Access</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>set</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Default Value</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>10000</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Units</term>

                  <listitem>
                    <para>Numerical objective-value units per elastic-residual unit; dimensionless for consistently nondimensional objective and residuals</para>
                  </listitem>
                </varlistentry>

                <varlistentry>
                  <term>Interfaces</term>

